summary:
  The relayed-Ogg reader looks for the artist without the chain headers that
  bound the newest title's comment block, so a title-only block borrows the
  previous track's artist and a later artist-only block reaches back.

history:
  Ogg-family streams carry the track in vorbis comments, and a reconnecting
  upstream writes a fresh block at every chain start. The first fix at this
  spot, 2026-09-06, anchored the artist search on the PREVIOUS TITLE — which
  separates blocks only when they spell ARTIST before TITLE. In the other
  order the old artist sits between the two titles, inside the window, and
  was taken for the new track: the very pairing the fix was written to end.
  Found 2026-09-08, before release. The boundary is the identification header
  an Ogg chain restart writes (\x03vorbis, OpusTags, \x7fFLAC and kin), and
  the window is closed at BOTH ends so a later artist-only block cannot reach
  back either.

target:
  package/contents/ui/reader.py

find:
          for mark in _OGG_BLOCK_MARKS:

replace:
          for mark in ():

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_reader_oggbuf.py::test_a_block_that_spells_title_before_artist_keeps_them_apart
  and tests/test_reader_oggbuf.py::test_a_later_artist_without_a_title_cannot_reach_back.
  Line-neutral.
